  "title": "Mary S NDE 4506",
  "date": "'July, 1963'",
  "content": "I was ten years old and swimming in a public pool (couldn't swim well). I got confused, swam into deeper water, and started to panic. Trying to yell 'help' I just choked down more water. It was very scared and exhausted. Then all of a sudden, such peace came over me it was wonderful. I could see my arms floating in the water - I was above. A lifeguard finally got to me (I don't remember this part) but when he got me out of the water I could see my body in his arms. My swimsuit top was pulled up and I saw him pull it down for me. (Later this was verified.) I came to in the first aid room - I'm sure after they did something to me. They kept asking me my name and I wouldn't tell them - so they thought I had some kind of damage, until they convinced me I wasn't in trouble (remember I was only ten). This experience has been with me all my life and I have been so interested in NDE and the afterlife since. I didn't get far enough to see a light or a tunnel. But I can still remember the life going before me - it was weird because it played every second I lived and it spun by so fast but it was like I was experiencing every second again, not just seeing it.",
